In terms of feasibility, a study from India compared prices of antihypertensive single-pill combinations and equivalent single-agent pills in the private health care sector. The results suggested that manufacturers have priced the combination higher than the price of its components. These data demonstrate that the price of combination pills could be lowered to match the combined price of 
